Day 19: String Reverser + Case Converter Tool

Concepts used:
 string methods —
 .upper(),
 .lower(),
 .title(),
 .swapcase(),
 slicing

Problem Statement

Write a Python program with a menu:
1. Reverse the string
2. Convert to UPPERCASE
3. Convert to lowercase
4. Convert to Title Case
5. Swap case (upper↔lower for each letter)
6. Exit


Ask the user to enter a string once, then let them apply any of these operations (looping back to the menu after each one) until they choose Exit.
New string methods
text = "Hello World"
text.upper()      # → "HELLO WORLD"
text.lower()       # → "hello world"
text.title()       # → "Hello World"  (capitalizes first letter of each word)
text.swapcase()    # → "hELLO wORLD"  (flips case of every letter)
text[::-1]         # → "dlroW olleH"  (reverse, from Day 16)


Example Run
Enter a string: Hello World
1. Reverse
2. UPPERCASE
3. lowercase
4. Title Case
5. Swap Case
6. Exit
Choose: 5
hELLO wORLD

Bonus (optional)
1.Let the user enter a new string each time they return to the menu, instead of being stuck with the same one (i.e., add an option for that, or ask fresh each loop).
2.Count and show how many uppercase and lowercase letters are in the string.
